===Etymology===
From {{der|en|ar|دِينَار}} and {{der|en|sh|динар}} (also from the Arabic), derived from the {{der|en|la|dēnārius}}. {{doublet|en|denarius}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|en|/ˈdiːnɑː(ɹ)/}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# The official [[currency]] of several countries, including [[Algeria]], [[Bahrain]], [[Iraq]], [[Jordan]], [[Kuwait]], [[Libya]], [[North Macedonia]], [[Serbia]] and [[Tunisia]].
# {{lb|en|historical}} An ancient [[Arab]] [[gold]] [[coin]] of 65 [[grain]]s in weight.

